---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Financial Overview">
	<div class="mb-12">
		<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4">Financial Overview</h1>
		<p class="text-lg text-slate-600 max-w-3xl">
			Transparent access to our community's financial health. We translate complex HOA financial documents into clear, easy-to-understand takeaways.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="space-y-12">
		<!-- Health Indicator & Overall Recommendation -->
		<section class="bg-blue-50 rounded-3xl p-8 border border-blue-100 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden">
			<!-- Decorative background element -->
			<div class="absolute top-0 right-0 -mt-4 -mr-4 w-32 h-32 bg-blue-200 rounded-full mix-blend-multiply filter blur-2xl opacity-50 pointer-events-none"></div>
			
			<div class="relative z-10 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 items-start md:items-center">
				<div class="flex-shrink-0 bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-blue-100 text-center md:w-48">
					<div class="text-5xl mb-2">🌟</div>
					<div class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">Overall Rating</div>
					<div class="text-xl font-bold text-green-600">Very Healthy</div>
				</div>
				
				<div class="flex-grow">
					<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-3">Strong Footing for the Future</h2>
					<p class="text-blue-900 mb-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">Owners are inheriting a very healthy, heavily funded Association. Homeowners should continue to break down their boxes (to prevent a repeat of 2025's $400+ emergency trash chute calls) and monitor "Elevator Extras" to ensure the brand-new elevators aren't developing chronic issues outside of their warranty and standard maintenance contracts.</p>
					
					<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
						<div class="bg-white/70 rounded-xl px-4 py-3 border border-blue-200/60 flex items-center gap-3 shadow-sm">
							<div class="bg-green-100 text-green-600 rounded-full w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center font-bold">✓</div>
							<div>
								<span class="block text-xs font-semibold text-blue-800 uppercase">2026 Assessments</span>
								<span class="block font-bold text-blue-900">Remaining Stable</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="bg-white/70 rounded-xl px-4 py-3 border border-blue-200/60 flex items-center gap-3 shadow-sm">
							<div class="bg-green-100 text-green-600 rounded-full w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center font-bold">✓</div>
							<div>
								<span class="block text-xs font-semibold text-blue-800 uppercase">Reserves Funding</span>
								<span class="block font-bold text-blue-900">Strong Allocation</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Independent Analysis Note -->
			<div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-blue-200/50 relative z-10">
				<p class="text-xs text-blue-800/60 italic leading-relaxed">
					<strong class="text-blue-900/80">Note:</strong> This analysis is independently conducted to ingest association financial statements and budgets for community transparency.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- VISUAL AIDS FOR INCOME & SPENDING -->
		<section>
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 border-b pb-2 mb-6">2025 Year-in-Review & Q1 2026 Liquidity Update</h2>
			<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
				
				<!-- 2025 Wrap-Up Card -->
				<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 p-6 flex flex-col">
					<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">2025 Closed Strong</h3>
					<div class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-green-600 mb-3">$134,643.52</div>
					<p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">The HOA finished its 2025 fiscal year in an excellent position, boasting a final net income of <strong>$134,643.52</strong>.</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Q1 2026 Run Rate Card -->
				<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 p-6 flex flex-col">
					<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3 flex justify-between items-end">
						<span>Q1 2026 Surplus</span>
						<span class="text-2xl text-green-700">+$11,950.19</span>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Through the first three months of 2026, the HOA is running a healthy surplus. Total operating expenses for the quarter were <strong>$219,383.20</strong>, which is over <strong>$44,000 under the anticipated budget</strong>.</p>
					
					<div class="mt-auto border-t pt-4">
						<div class="flex justify-between text-sm font-semibold mb-1">
							<span class="text-slate-700">Current Assets (As of March 31, 2026)</span>
							<span class="text-blue-700">$358,999.09</span>
						</div>
						<p class="text-xs text-slate-500">The Association's total assets stand at a highly robust level.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Savings Card -->
				<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 p-6 flex flex-col justify-center text-center">
					<div class="w-16 h-16 bg-blue-50 text-blue-600 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center text-3xl mx-auto mb-4 border border-blue-100 shadow-sm">
						🏦
					</div>
					<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Saving for the Future</h3>
					<div class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-blue-600 mb-3">$128,195.68</div>
					<p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed px-4 mb-3">Total recognized reserve balance as of March. The Association faithfully transfers <strong>$21,365.92</strong> into reserve accounts each month.</p>
					<div class="bg-blue-50 text-blue-800 text-xs font-medium px-3 py-2 rounded-lg inline-block text-left">
						<strong>Note:</strong> Management is currently holding about $124,000 of these reserve funds in the operating account and is in the process of officially transferring the cash to the dedicated Reserve bank account.
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Spending Summary Card (Q1 2026 Monthly Averages) -->
				<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 p-6 flex flex-col lg:col-span-2">
					<div class="mb-5">
						<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Key Spending Categories (Q1 2026 Monthly Averages)</h3>
						<p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
							First-time homeowners need to understand the difference between the HOA's stable, contracted monthly burn rate and the variable expenses that fluctuate based on building usage and repairs. Here is where the money is going, based on the first three months of 2026:
						</p>
					</div>
					
					<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
						<!-- Fixed Contracts -->
						<div>
							<h4 class="font-bold text-blue-900 border-b border-slate-200 pb-2 mb-3">Fixed/Contracted Expenses (The Stable Burn Rate)</h4>
							<p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-4 leading-relaxed">These are the predictable, recurring monthly bills that keep the building insured, managed, and legally compliant:</p>
							<ul class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start border-b border-slate-50 pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Reserve Savings</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Faithfully transferred into our dedicated savings account.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$21,374.00</span>
								</li>
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start border-b border-slate-50 pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Insurance</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Amortized portion of our $143,885 annual premium.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$12,021.08</span>
								</li>
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start border-b border-slate-50 pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Management Contract</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Paid to Action Property Management.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$6,000.00</span>
								</li>
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start border-b border-slate-50 pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Janitorial Contract</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Standard building cleaning services.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$5,816.42</span>
								</li>
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start border-b border-slate-50 pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Elevator Contract</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Standard maintenance with Otis Elevator Company.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$1,701.20</span>
								</li>
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Landscape Contract</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Standard groundskeeping with BrightView Landscape Services.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$1,530.00</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<!-- Variable Expenditures -->
						<div>
							<h4 class="font-bold text-orange-900 border-b border-slate-200 pb-2 mb-3">Variable & Additional Expenditures (The Fluctuating Costs)</h4>
							<p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-4 leading-relaxed">These categories represent utilities and out-of-scope maintenance that spiked in early 2026. The amounts below represent the average monthly spend over the first quarter:</p>
							<ul class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start border-b border-slate-50 pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Expected Net Utilities <span class="font-normal text-xs">(Water, Electricity, Refuse)</span></span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Our gross utility bills currently average $21,268.06 per month. However, residents directly reimburse the HOA for individual water submetering. While early 2026 collections are lagging due to rollouts and unsold units, the fully occupied budgeted reimbursement is $15,855.25 per month. When fully realized, this drops the true expected net utility cost to the HOA to just $5,412.81 a month.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$5,412.81</span>
								</li>
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start border-b border-slate-50 pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Elevator Repairs & Extras</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">This reflects a massive $7,478.00 in unbudgeted, out-of-scope elevator repairs and extras in Q1.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$2,492.67</span>
								</li>
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start border-b border-slate-50 pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Access Control & Security</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Driven by $2,666.37 in YTD vendor dispatch and monitoring fees.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$888.79</span>
								</li>
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start border-b border-slate-50 pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Janitorial Extras & Supplies</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Driven by $2,363.95 in unbudgeted extra trash pull-outs and supply restocks.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$787.98</span>
								</li>
								<li class="flex justify-between items-start pb-2">
									<div class="pr-4">
										<span class="font-semibold block text-slate-800">Plumbing & Sewer Repairs</span>
										<span class="text-xs text-slate-500 block mt-1">Driven by $2,314.62 in early 2026 vendor calls for pipe and sewer line clearing.</span>
									</div>
									<span class="font-bold text-slate-900 whitespace-nowrap">$771.54</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- FINANCIAL VISUALIZATION -->
		<section>
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 border-b pb-2 mb-6">Financial Visualization (June 2025 - March 2026)</h2>
			
			<!-- Chart Container -->
			<div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-6 mb-8">
				<div class="flex-1 bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 p-6">
					<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 text-center">Monthly Income</h3>
					<div class="relative w-full h-80">
						<canvas id="incomeChart"></canvas>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="flex-1 bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 p-6">
					<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 text-center">Monthly Expenses</h3>
					<div class="relative w-full h-80">
						<canvas id="expenseChart"></canvas>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Data Table -->
			<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 overflow-x-auto">
				<table class="w-full text-sm text-left whitespace-nowrap">
					<thead class="text-xs text-slate-700 uppercase bg-slate-50 border-b border-slate-200">
						<tr>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold">Month</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold bg-green-50/50">Total Income</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-500">Member Dues</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-500">Developer Dues</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold bg-rose-50/50">Total Expenses</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-500">Mgmt/Admin</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-500">Maintenance</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-500">Elevator</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-500">Utilities</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-500">Insurance</th>
							<th class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-500">Reserves</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 text-slate-600" id="financialTableBody">
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			
			<div class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-600 bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
				<strong>* Note on Developer Subsidization:</strong> Developer dues have been reclassified into member dues starting in November 2025. Developers continue to faithfully pay for unsold units; these payments are now seamlessly merged directly into the main assessment revenue line.
			</div>
		</section>

		<script is:inline src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
		<script is:inline>
			(function() {
				const financialData = [
					{ month: 'Jun 2025', income: { member: 5524, developer: 67692 }, expenses: { admin: 13199, maintenance: 7658, elevator: 0, utilities: 3103, insurance: 0, reserves: 21366 } },
					{ month: 'Jul 2025', income: { member: 10925, developer: 62591 }, expenses: { admin: 4071, maintenance: 4734, elevator: 0, utilities: 1935, insurance: 0, reserves: 21366 } },
					{ month: 'Aug 2025', income: { member: 19104, developer: 55178 }, expenses: { admin: 3503, maintenance: 2450, elevator: 6075, utilities: 8766, insurance: 0, reserves: 21366 } },
					{ month: 'Sep 2025', income: { member: 30507, developer: 42858 }, expenses: { admin: 3500, maintenance: 7825, elevator: 0, utilities: 13835, insurance: 0, reserves: 21366 } },
					{ month: 'Oct 2025', income: { member: 34259, developer: 39520 }, expenses: { admin: 15000, maintenance: 8072, elevator: 0, utilities: 16778, insurance: 0, reserves: 21366 } },
					{ month: 'Nov 2025*', income: { member: 72180, developer: 0 }, expenses: { admin: 7500, maintenance: 3350, elevator: 0, utilities: 22150, insurance: 0, reserves: 21366 } },
					{ month: 'Dec 2025*', income: { member: 87557, developer: 0 }, expenses: { admin: 19603, maintenance: 11064, elevator: 6425, utilities: 30957, insurance: 12021, reserves: 21366 } },
					{ month: 'Jan 2026', income: { member: 70501, developer: 0 }, expenses: { admin: 17684, maintenance: 2173, elevator: 3402, utilities: 19836, insurance: 11654, reserves: 21368 } },
					{ month: 'Feb 2026', income: { member: 73080, developer: 0 }, expenses: { admin: 21343, maintenance: 1641, elevator: 0, utilities: 22626, insurance: 12021, reserves: 21375 } },
					{ month: 'Mar 2026', income: { member: 71716, developer: 0 }, expenses: { admin: 19720, maintenance: 10735, elevator: 9179, utilities: 21343, insurance: 12021, reserves: 21383 } }
				];

				const initCharts = () => {
					if (typeof Chart === 'undefined') return setTimeout(initCharts, 50);
					
					const labels = financialData.map(d => d.month);
					const formatCurrency = (val) => new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD', maximumFractionDigits: 0 }).format(val);

					const incomeCtx = document.getElementById('incomeChart');
					if (incomeCtx && !incomeCtx.dataset.rendered) {
						incomeCtx.dataset.rendered = "true";
						new Chart(incomeCtx, {
							type: 'bar',
							data: {
								labels: labels,
								datasets: [
									{ label: 'Member Dues', data: financialData.map(d => d.income.member), backgroundColor: '#3b82f6' },
									{ label: 'Developer Dues', data: financialData.map(d => d.income.developer), backgroundColor: '#8b5cf6' }
								]
							},
							options: {
								responsive: true, maintainAspectRatio: false,
								plugins: {
									tooltip: {
										callbacks: {
											label: function(context) {
												const val = context.raw;
												let total = 0;
												context.chart.data.datasets.forEach((ds, idx) => { if (context.chart.isDatasetVisible(idx)) total += ds.data[context.dataIndex]; });
												const pct = total !== 0 ? Math.round((Math.abs(val) / Math.abs(total)) * 100) : 0;
												return `${context.dataset.label}: ${formatCurrency(val)} (${pct}%)`;
											}
										}
									}
								},
								scales: { x: { stacked: true }, y: { stacked: true, ticks: { callback: function(val) { return '$' + val / 1000 + 'k'; } } } }
							}
						});
					}

					const expenseCtx = document.getElementById('expenseChart');
					if (expenseCtx && !expenseCtx.dataset.rendered) {
						expenseCtx.dataset.rendered = "true";
						new Chart(expenseCtx, {
							type: 'bar',
							data: {
								labels: labels,
								datasets: [
									{ label: 'Reserves', data: financialData.map(d => d.expenses.reserves), backgroundColor: '#3b82f6' },
									{ label: 'Insurance', data: financialData.map(d => d.expenses.insurance), backgroundColor: '#10b981' },
									{ label: 'Management/Admin', data: financialData.map(d => d.expenses.admin), backgroundColor: '#8b5cf6' },
									{ label: 'Utilities', data: financialData.map(d => d.expenses.utilities), backgroundColor: '#06b6d4' },
									{ label: 'Maintenance', data: financialData.map(d => d.expenses.maintenance), backgroundColor: '#f59e0b' },
									{ label: 'Elevator', data: financialData.map(d => d.expenses.elevator), backgroundColor: '#ef4444' }
								]
							},
							options: {
								responsive: true, maintainAspectRatio: false,
								plugins: {
									tooltip: {
										callbacks: {
											label: function(context) {
												const val = context.raw;
												let total = 0;
												context.chart.data.datasets.forEach((ds, idx) => { if (context.chart.isDatasetVisible(idx)) total += ds.data[context.dataIndex]; });
												const pct = total !== 0 ? Math.round((val / total) * 100) : 0;
												return `${context.dataset.label}: ${formatCurrency(val)} (${pct}%)`;
											}
										}
									}
								},
								scales: { x: { stacked: true }, y: { stacked: true, ticks: { callback: function(val) { return '$' + val / 1000 + 'k'; } } } }
							}
						});
					}

					const tbody = document.getElementById('financialTableBody');
					if (tbody && !tbody.dataset.rendered) {
						tbody.dataset.rendered = "true";
						financialData.forEach(d => {
							const totalIncome = d.income.member + d.income.developer;
							const totalExpenses = d.expenses.admin + d.expenses.maintenance + d.expenses.elevator + d.expenses.utilities + d.expenses.insurance + d.expenses.reserves;
							
							const tr = document.createElement('tr');
							tr.className = "hover:bg-slate-50 transition-colors";
							tr.innerHTML = `
								<td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-slate-900 border-r border-slate-100">${d.month}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3 font-bold text-green-700 bg-green-50/30">${formatCurrency(totalIncome)}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3">${formatCurrency(d.income.member)}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3 border-r border-slate-100">${formatCurrency(d.income.developer)}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3 font-bold text-rose-700 bg-rose-50/30">${formatCurrency(totalExpenses)}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3">${formatCurrency(d.expenses.admin)}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3">${formatCurrency(d.expenses.maintenance)}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3">${formatCurrency(d.expenses.elevator)}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3">${formatCurrency(d.expenses.utilities)}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3">${formatCurrency(d.expenses.insurance)}</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-3">${formatCurrency(d.expenses.reserves)}</td>
							`;
							tbody.appendChild(tr);
						});
					}
				};
				
				if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
					document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', initCharts);
				} else {
					initCharts();
				}
				document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initCharts);
			})();
		</script>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 border-b pb-2 mb-6">6 Key Financial Trends (June 2025 - March 2026)</h2>
			<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
				<!-- Card 1 -->
				<div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 flex flex-col hover:bg-slate-100 transition-colors">
					<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
						<div class="w-10 h-10 bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-600 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-xl shadow-sm">🏢</div>
						<h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 leading-tight">Developer Subsidization (The Safety Net)</h3>
					</div>
					<p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-3"><strong>The Trend:</strong> Because units in the building sold slower than initially anticipated, the developer has been legally required to pay assessments on all unsold units.</p>
